WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.135
Govern is central in CSF 2.0 because it describes how cybersecurity risk management is directed, prioritized, and overseen.

2
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:12.020
It connects cybersecurity to enterprise risk.

3
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:17.309
That connection matters because cybersecurity is not only a technical activity.

4
00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:23.560
It affects operations, finance, legal obligations, customers, safety, suppliers, reputation, and mission delivery.

5
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:31.253
Govern helps an organization decide why security matters, who owns decisions, and how risk is communicated.

6
00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:37.984
Govern includes strategy, policy, roles, responsibilities, authority, oversight, organizational context, and risk management expectations.

7
00:00:37.984 --> 00:00:42.792
Good governance does not mean paperwork for its own sake.

8
00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:52.889
It means the right people understand their role, the right owners can make decisions, and teams know how priorities are set.

9
00:00:52.889 --> 00:01:03.467
Without governance, technical teams may collect evidence and build controls, but still lack a clear path for exceptions, tradeoffs, funding, and accountability.

10
00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:08.756
Supply chain risk is also part of CSF 2.0 governance.

11
00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:15.007
Organizations rely on vendors, cloud providers, software suppliers, service providers, contractors, and partners.

12
00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:23.180
A supplier can affect cybersecurity risk even when the system is not directly owned by the organization.

13
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:33.277
Governance should clarify who evaluates supplier risk, how requirements are communicated, what evidence is needed, and how supplier issues are tracked.

14
00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:36.162
Govern makes the other Functions actionable.

15
00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:42.413
Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, and Recover all require priorities, owners, policies, and oversight.

16
00:01:42.413 --> 00:01:48.663
When governance is weak, the framework can become a list of disconnected tasks.

17
00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:57.318
When governance is clear, CSF 2.0 becomes a decision system for setting direction and managing risk responsibly.
